 "name": "finish_ti64_anodize_blue_35v",
 "note": "Ti-6Al-4V appearance from literature complex IOR (Ti n,k at 650/550/450 nm -> normal-incidence F0; F82 tint). Not a measured coating. Physically based visualization under stated material assumptions. Type-II/III style Ti anodize as a single TiO2 thin film (IOR 2.4) on Ti-6Al-4V (Blender 4.2's Thin Film input does not act on metals, so anodize.py evaluates a normal/82-degree thin-film model of air/TiO2/Ti and bakes the interference colour into the conductor F0 + F82 tint of the anodized regions). Interference colour depends on oxide thickness; nominal voltages follow common shop colour charts, thicknesses were picked from a normal-incidence thin-film model so the colour matches the chart (~2.2-2.5 nm/V above ~30 V, sub-linear below). appearance_assumed, not a measured coating. Handle/ring/pad/spine anodized; bevel, edge apex and serrations stay raw bright Ti (they are ground after anodizing on real knives). Signature (maker's mark) is still mixed over every slot last.",
